      "summary": ": Today at Cardrona 21 August 2026 — It's a fine day up here, with a little more cloud and wind expected to roll in later this afternoon ahead of tomorrow's front. Snow conditions are all-time after a few cold days — the snowmaking guns have been keeping things fresh and the groomers have laid down some sweet corduroy. Grab the sunscreen before heading out and make the most of it before the storm arrives. Main Basin lifts run from 8:30am, with Captains, T-Bar, Soho and Willows following from 9am, and Pipe and Platter opening from 8am. Kindy Conveyor, Learner Conveyors, McDougall's Chondola, Whitestar Express, Valley View, Captains Express, T-Bar, Soho Express and Willow's Quad are all running today — only Wells Pipe Platter is closed. Learners Slope, Main Basin, Captains, Soho, Little Willows, Big Willows, Arcadia Chutes and Summit are all open for skiing, along with ski touring access, though Mt Cardrona itself is closed. Baby Bucks, Little Bucks, Antlers Alley, Stag Lane, Big Bucks and Gravity Cross are all open in the park, while Peoples Pipe, Olympic Pipe and Big Air remain closed. Hawea Flat and Holy Family Ski Schools are up on the mountain today too. The road is chain-free right now, but chains must still be carried, and there's an active road hazard advisory on the access roads — check that before you head up. Car Parks A and B are full, but C, the Yard, Valley View and the Pines all have space. If you're grabbing lunch, dodge the 1pm rush or book a table at the Mezz.",
